  "hist_multiples_note": "Trailing averages of the forward multiples, the model's equivalent of FactSet's FE_VALUATION(PE | FFEV_EBITDA, MEAN, NTM4_ROLL) averaged over -1AY/-3AY/-5AY to NOW: weekly observations over five years, each dated at the last US trading day of its week (FactSet Global Prices close in USD, calendar US, so a holiday Friday is dated at the Thursday instead of lost), paired with the FactSet Estimates NTM consensus mean sampled weekly (the latest on or before the price date, within 6 days). NTM P/E = close / NTM EPS. NTM EV/EBITDA = (close x common shares outstanding of the latest fiscal quarter ended on or before the date, FactSet Fundamentals FF_COM_SHS_OUT, the company-level count across every share class, + that quarter's FF_NET_DEBT) / NTM EBITDA. y1/y3/y5 = simple means of the observations dated within the last 52/156/260 weeks ending at as_of (n = observations counted; a week is skipped when an input is missing or the denominator is not positive); spot_last_week = the ratio at as_of; not point-in-time (shares and net debt as later reported). shares_basis records the share count used: the security-level shares_outstanding endpoint is one class only for Alphabet (Class A) and Workday and halved Alphabet's historical EV until 2026-10-09. Refreshed nightly by the FactSet routine (step k of tools/oracle/FACTSET-PROMPT.md).",
  "hist_multiples_as_of": "2026-10-23",
  "hist_multiples_fetched": "2026-10-23",
  "market_cap_note": "Market values are priced at the close the snapshot carries: market_cap_usd_m = price x shares_m and market_cap_date = price_date, where shares_m is FactSet Fundamentals FF_COM_SHS_OUT of the latest reported fiscal quarter (shares_date; the company-level count across every share class, the same count the weekly history uses). market_value_factset is the market_value endpoint's figure for the audit only: it posts a session's value only hours after the 19:58 New York routine runs (at 8 PM New York on 2026-10-08 it still carried the 7-Oct value) and for Alphabet it counts the listed classes only (A + C), so it is never copied as the market cap (owner, 2026-10-09: tables 22 and 23 always at the prior close).",
  "adtv_note": "ADTV = average daily traded value over the last three months in US$ million: the mean of FactSet Global Prices daily turnover (volume x VWAP, USD) over the trading days of the window ending at price_date (equivalent to AVERAGE of P_VOLUME x XP_PRICE_VWAP day by day); product_of_averages_usd_m is the owner's Excel cross-check, P_VOLUME_AVG(-3AM,0) x AVERAGE(XP_PRICE_VWAP(0,-3AM,,,,USD)).",
  "refresh_note": "Refreshed nightly at 7:58 PM New York time by the Claude Routine 'FNAM Oracle: FactSet nightly refresh' (prompt in tools/oracle/FACTSET-PROMPT.md): prices are the latest completed session's close (the prior close for a page read the next morning), consensus as of the run date.",
  "price_series_fetched": "2026-10-23",
  "price_series_note": "prices_orcl_factset.csv = ORCL daily OHLC and volume from FactSet Global Prices (USD, split-adjusted), 2015-01-02 onward, merged nightly by the routine (step g); the page's price authority for every date it covers. The runner's Nasdaq/Yahoo/Stooq series (prices_orcl_daily.csv) fills only the dates FactSet has not posted yet."
